## Primary Directive

You MUST create a new implementation plan for deliverable {{DeliverableId}}.
You MUST use the devstack get_deliverable tool to read the details.
If the tool is unavailable, you MUST STOP.
This prompt is for AI-to-AI communication and automated processing.
You MUST interpret each instruction literally.
You MUST NOT seek human clarification.

## RFC 2119 Requirement Rules

You MUST use RFC 2119 keywords in uppercase.
Use MUST and REQUIRED for absolute requirements.
Use MUST NOT and SHALL NOT for absolute prohibitions.
Use SHOULD and RECOMMENDED for strong guidance.
Use SHOULD NOT and NOT RECOMMENDED for cautionary guidance.
Use MAY and OPTIONAL for truly optional items.

## ASD-STE100 Writing Rules

You MUST write in clear, direct English.
Keep instructions under 30 words.
Keep descriptive text under 45 words.
Use active voice.
Use direct commands.
Use one word for one meaning.
Break complex work into short ordered lists.

## Core Requirements

You MUST create plans that AI agents or humans can execute.
You MUST use deterministic language.
You MUST avoid ambiguity.
You MUST structure content for automated parsing.
You MUST keep each plan self-contained.
You MUST NOT depend on outside context.

## Plan Structure Requirements

You MUST make each plan consist of atomic tasks.
Each task MUST be processable alone unless dependencies are declared.
Each task SHOULD have measurable completion criteria.
Tasks SHOULD run in parallel when no dependency exists.
Each task MUST include an exact file path.
Each task MUST include the relevant function or symbol.
Each task MUST include exact implementation requirements.
You MUST NOT leave any task open to interpretation.

## Output Requirements

You MUST produce machine-readable output.
You MUST use deterministic structure.
You MUST make the plan suitable for autonomous execution.
You SHOULD use all available deliverable fields.
You MAY skip fields that do not apply.
You MUST use the update_deliverable tool to update the deliverable.
If architecture or technology choices are ambiguous, you MUST set the deliverable state to NeedsReview.
You MUST then use the update_deliverable tool to add AgentFeedback.
You MUST STOP after that update.
You MUST use the create_task tool with ProjectId and DeliverableId.
You MUST set the deliverable status to IMPLEMENT.
You MUST NOT edit files or make other changes.
